    {
      "type": "post",
      "id": "7445420845767974912",
      "entityId": "7445420845767974912",
      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/stuart-hardman_ok-its-not-friday-but-theres-a-bank-holiday-activity-7445420845767974912-n2_D",
      "shareLinkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7445420844635320321",
      "shareUrn": "urn:li:share:7445420844635320321",
      "content": "Ok, it's not Friday, but there's a bank holiday tomorrow so today is as good as a Friday and I need to get this 𝙵̶𝚛̶𝚒̶𝚍̶𝚊̶𝚢̶ Thursday Rant off my chest.\n\nBring out the klaxon...\n\n🚨🚨Thursday Rant🚨🚨\n\nWe're all aware of 'shrinkflation' the ever decreasing size of various grocery items:\n📉 Tins of Quality Street getting ever smaller\n📉 King Size Mars Bars that are now the size of Fun Size from when we were kids\n📉 Grab bags of crisps that are well, normal size packs of crisps\n\nI have a modicum of acceptance of some of these. You may have one or two less sweets or crisps and it helps with the waist size. But... I saw an abomination in Tesco last night. One that really triggered my mild OCD.\n\nLook at number of tea bags in the boxes in the image below. Look closely.\n🫖 Small box - 40 tea bags - perfectly reasonable\n🫖 Large box - 160 tea bags - pretty standard\n🫖 Medium box - 70 (SEVENTY!) tea bags - WHAT ARE YOU DOING!\n\nI don't know about you but shrinkflation isn't going to make me have less cups of tea in a day so reducing the box size does absolutely nothing, I'm just going to buy more boxes which in all likelihood means more packaging waste. Just put the prices up a bit!!\n\nSeventy tea bags, i'm still shaking my head. Have them in neat multiples.\n\nAnyway, if you're a business contemplating shrinkflation perhaps making other areas of your business more efficient could stop you upsetting your customers with random quantities of items in boxes.\n\nIf you need a more efficient cloud based ERP system to help you manage your costs and get better control of your business and you want it in quick then get in contact and let me help you.",
