      "type": "post",
      "id": "7432837400743161856",
      "entityId": "7432837400743161856",
      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/stuart-hardman_whats-your-website-going-to-be-called-mike-activity-7432837400743161856-ZkZ8",
      "shareLinkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7432837399891783681",
      "shareUrn": "urn:li:share:7432837399891783681",
      "content": "Domain names - do you need them for your business?\n\nI was having a chat with someone today that are setting up a new company, they've picked the name, registered the company but the .com domain for their actual company name isn't available.\n\nInstead they've picked a hyphenated domain and chosen an extended form of part of their company name with a .com on the end, so it's not really their company name at all but they've also got the .co.uk version of \"not their company name\"\n\nThey're UK based so I checked the obvious and their exact company name .co.uk was available, for less than £4 per year. They're aware and didn't want it.\n\nThis isn't my area of expertise but admit to being a bit puzzled. It brought to mind the video below.\n\nWould you go for the .co.uk for your actual company name or ignore it entirely?\n\nhttps://lnkd.in/eYXAtVcM",
